# JML Process Flow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    HR[HR/Manager Request] -->|New hire| J1[Joiner.ps1]
    HR -->|Role or dept change| M1[Mover.ps1]
    HR -->|Termination| L1[Leaver.ps1]

    J1 --> J2[Create Entra user]
    J2 --> J3[Assign license]
    J3 --> J4[Add role-based groups]
    J4 --> J5[Set manager]
    J5 --> AUDIT[(jml-audit-log.csv)]

    M1 --> M2[Update job title / dept]
    M2 --> M3[Remove old-role groups]
    M3 --> M4[Add new-role groups]
    M4 --> M5[Update manager]
    M5 --> AUDIT

    L1 --> L2[Disable sign-in]
    L2 --> L3[Revoke active sessions]
    L3 --> L4[Remove licenses]
    L4 --> L5[Remove from all groups]
    L5 --> L6[Add to Leavers-Audit group]
    L6 --> L7[Stamp termination date]
    L7 --> AUDIT
    L7 -.->|After retention window| DEL[Manual hard-delete]
```

**Design note on Leaver ordering:** disable + revoke sessions happen before any
license or group cleanup. If the script fails partway through, the account is
already locked out — the remaining steps are hygiene, not security-critical.
